---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import { site, hasContact } from "../site";

const all = await getCollection("prizes");
const makers = new Set(all.map((e) => e.data.manufacturer));
---

<Layout
  title="About Centre Pullz — what this database is and where the data comes from"
  description="Centre Pullz collects crane-game prize centre-of-gravity measurements published by Merry☆An on X, translates them into English and Simplified Chinese, and adds plain-language play notes."
>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <span class="eyebrow">About · 关于</span>
    <h1>About Centre Pullz</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Centre Pullz is a free, bilingual reference for crane-game (UFO catcher)
      prize physics: {all.length} prize boxes from {makers.size} manufacturers,
      each with its measured weight and centre of gravity.
    </p>

    <h2>Where the measurements come from</h2>
    <p>
      Every measurement on this site was taken and published by
      <a href={site.sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Merry☆An ({site.sourceHandle})</a>,
      who weighs and measures prize boxes and posts the results on X under the
      tag <span class="mono">#重心情報</span>. Centre Pullz is not affiliated with
      Merry☆An — it collects those posts, structures them, and translates them.
    </p>
    <p>
      Each entry links back to the original post. If you find this data useful,
      the credit belongs there.
    </p>

    <h2>What this site adds</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Translation.</strong> The source posts are in Japanese. Every
        entry is translated into English and Simplified Chinese, keeping the
        original Japanese title intact.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Structure.</strong> Measurements are normalised into consistent
        fields — figure size, box weight, box dimensions, and one line per
        measured axis — so entries can be compared and searched.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Play notes.</strong> Each entry ends with a suggested approach
        written by an AI model from that entry's measurements. These are clearly
        labelled and are commentary, not expert instruction. See the
        <a href="/guide/">guide</a> for how much weight to give them.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Images</h2>
    <p>
      Prize photographs are the manufacturers' own official product images
      (Banpresto, Furyu, Sega, Taito and others), linked directly from the
      manufacturers' websites rather than copied onto this server. The annotated
      measurement diagrams are Merry☆An's own photographs, credited on each entry.
      If you hold rights to an image used here and want it removed, see
      <a href="/terms/">Terms</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>How it's built</h2>
    <p>
      A static site — no accounts, no user-generated content, no database server.
      Each prize is a plain text file validated at build time, which is why the
      fields stay consistent. New measurements are collected and added on a
      recurring schedule.
    </p>

    <h2>Corrections and contact</h2>
    <p>
      Measurements are transcribed from public posts and can contain transcription
      errors, and the source posts themselves note that prizes vary unit to unit.
      If something looks wrong, corrections are welcome.
    </p>
    {hasContact ? (
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/">Send a correction or question →</a>
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p class="mono note">
        A contact method for this site has not been published yet.
      </p>
    )}

    <p class="next">
      <a class="btn" href="/database/">Search the database →</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .note {
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .next {
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
</style>
